From db0679ae0198632f17931901f9de5a93326f45a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:30:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Import screen lists every manifest; USA category

- The import screen showed only eight manifests, so newer ones dropped off once more were on file. It now lists up to sixty, newest saved first, loaded in parallel
- Manifests whose entries are all live are folded into an 'Already imported' section; each card shows its file name
- 'usa' added as a category for studies of the United States as a whole
---
 docs/WEEKLY_PIPELINE.md               |  2 +-
 src/components/admin/WeeklyImport.tsx | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 src/lib/admin/importActions.ts        | 15 ++++++++++-----
 src/lib/data.ts                       |  2 ++
 src/lib/weekly/manifest.ts            |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/WEEKLY_PIPELINE.md b/docs/WEEKLY_PIPELINE.md
index ae83bd9..71a0c5d 100644
--- a/docs/WEEKLY_PIPELINE.md
+++ b/docs/WEEKLY_PIPELINE.md
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@ One JSON file per week. Whoever writes it — a person, Claude or HT+ — the im
 }
 ```
 
-- `territory`: `uae-gcc`, `south-africa`, `new-zealand`, `mauritius`, `north-carolina`, `singapore`, or `global` for a study that belongs to no single territory.
+- `territory`: `uae-gcc`, `south-africa`, `new-zealand`, `mauritius`, `north-carolina`, `singapore`, `global` for a study that belongs to no single territory, or `usa` for a study of the United States as a whole.
 - `week_label` uses FalconBridge's week number; `week_of` is the Monday the review period starts.
 - An entry may carry a scan, a report, or both. `files` need a report.
 - Slots and their default access: 1 User guide (pack), 2 Executive deck (pack), 3 Full research report (pack), 4 Executive summary (open), 5 Executive visual (open), 6 Reference and link audit (internal). `label` and `access` override the defaults. A slot left out is created empty and internal.
